  "summary": "Crafted for effortless cooking, this <b>one-pot red lentil soup</b> brings classic Indian warmth to your dinner table with minimal cleanup. The dish begins with a fragrant foundation of browned onions, garlic, ginger, and blooming spices like cumin and ground turmeric cooked in rich <b>golden ghee</b>. Quick-cooking red split lentils simmer directly in the same vessel along with crushed tomatoes and broth, absorbing every layer of aromatic flavor as they break down into a naturally silky texture. This simple method eliminates unnecessary pots while maximizing taste depth. A splash of freshly squeezed <b>lemon juice</b> at the very end brightens the earthy notes of the legumes, creating a comforting bowl that feels both nourishing and revitalizing. Ladle this aromatic soup into bowls and serve alongside warm naan or steamed basmati rice for a wholesome, protein-rich meal that satisfies the entire family on cold evenings.",
